xnu 0397: let the bitmap's free count unblock the allocator

Measured 2026-11-20 with the 0370 audit: the root reaches SpringBoard with
`total 4194304 counter 0 bitmap 574 diff 574`. `hfs_block_alloc_int` refuses
every allocation while the free-block counter is zero (`dskFulErr`), so no
write that needs a new block succeeds: `UMD_INIT` cannot write its keybags
(ENOSPC 28), SQLite cannot create /private/var/Keychains/keychain-2.db,
securityd answers SecItemAdd with errSecNotAvailable and bluetoothd aborts.

The bitmap is the authority on which blocks are free; the counter is a cache
that the old deallocation bug (0372) left at zero, and the blocks it lost are
gone from the bitmap too. Adopting the bitmap count at mount lets the
allocator use the blocks that are actually free. The correction only raises
the counter, and the audit line still prints both numbers.

diff --git a/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/VolumeAllocation.c b/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/VolumeAllocation.c
index a11add4..69a0f26 100644
--- a/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/VolumeAllocation.c
+++ b/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/VolumeAllocation.c
@@ -2008,6 +2008,18 @@ hfs_free_bitmap_audit(struct hfsmount *hfsmp)
 	printf("MONDRIAN HFSAUDIT: total %u counter %u bitmap %llu diff %lld\n",
 	    total, (unsigned)vcb->freeBlocks, freebits,
 	    (long long)freebits - (long long)vcb->freeBlocks);
+	/*
+	 * MONDRIAN: the bitmap is the authority on which blocks are free; the
+	 * counter is a cache that the old deallocation bug left at zero, and
+	 * hfs_block_alloc_int refuses every allocation while it is zero. Adopt
+	 * the bitmap count so the blocks that are actually free can be used.
+	 * The correction only raises the counter; a counter above the bitmap is
+	 * left alone for fsck to explain.
+	 */
+	if (freebits > (u_int64_t)vcb->freeBlocks &&
+	    freebits <= (u_int64_t)0xffffffffu) {
+		vcb->freeBlocks = (u_int32_t)freebits;
+	}
 }
 
 static OSErr ReadBitmapBlock(ExtendedVCB		*vcb,
